{"name":"Assassin","hex":"#2d4f83","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"assassin","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone who intentionally kills a person, especially a professional who kills a public or political figure.","Any ruthless killer."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To assassinate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assassin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Assassination","blocks":[{"text":"Assassination is the willful killing, by a sudden or secret attack, of a person—especially a prominent or important one—typically for political, social, or ideological reasons. Assassinations may be ordered by individuals or organizations, and carried out by themselves or their hired accomplices. Acts of assassination have been performed since ancient times. A person who carries out an assassination is called an assassin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Lincoln_assassination_slide_c1900_-_Restoration.jpg/330px-Lincoln_assassination_slide_c1900_-_Restoration.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assassination"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/The_Masyaf_Castle.jpg/500px-The_Masyaf_Castle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/The_Masyaf_Castle.jpg/1280px-The_Masyaf_Castle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/The_Masyaf_Castle.jpg/500px-The_Masyaf_Castle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Masyaf Castle in Hama, Syria. It was the headquarters of the Assassins in the Levant. Picture taken in 2017","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Masyaf_Castle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Moor